[  131.6s] - **products.amount_field**: OK. The API field is `overdue_cents`. "The API gives every amount in integer cents. Say euros; send cents." So amount_scale is 100, promise_scale is null and no rounding is needed.
[  131.6s] - **products.floor_field**: OK. "`min_due_cents` (card) or `instalment_cents` (loan)." Cards map to min_due_cents; cash and vehicle loans map to instalment_cents.
[  131.6s] - **products.floor_pct**: OK. Every floor is a named field, not a percentage, so null is right.
[  131.6s] - **products** (rest): OK. "credit card ending 7734", "cash loan", "vehicle loan" use `{card_end}`. list_field is accounts, id_field is account_ref, type_field is kind.
[  131.6s] - **bands**: OK, with one risk.
